{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1130948-beholding-an-awakening-in-progress","id":1130948,"title":"Beholding an Awakening in progress","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-18T13:40:03-07:00","id":1130948,"title":"Beholding an Awakening in progress","content":"Hi there folks.<br /> <br /> I'm currently directing a Mage game, and in the last session something unexpected happened - two players stumbled upon an Awakening in progress. The Acanthus-to-be was unconscious, in a coma-like state, so mistakenly taking it by a trance they reached into her mind, using <i><b>Dream Reaching (Mind 2)</b></i>.<br /> <br /> I thought it could be an interesting scene, so i'm willing to let them peak into the Supernal and see how the situation unfolds. As both of them are fairly new Mages, this experience could influence and shape them drastically, so its kind of a big deal. I'm thinking about ways to convey the experience, and i'm interested about your opinions on the matter. Has any of you described this kind of situation? How would you do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T13:48:55-07:00","id":1130957,"title":"","content":"Damn, SoS is supposed to cover this very thing.<br /> <br /> What are your players Paths? It might be their only chance to see Arcadia and it's symbols. I'd consider a Comdition or a minor, but permanent shift in the way they see things via Mage Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T14:20:47-07:00","id":1130972,"title":"","content":"Until &quot;Signs of Sorcery&quot; comes out we only have Forum posts and conjecture to work of off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1129690-awakening-relics?p=1129791#post1129791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Signs has a few more Awakening-only Merits that you can *only* buy when a character awakens (or, more usually, when creating them later in life) and a discussion of weird, &quot;metamorphic&quot; awakenings where the world you come back to isn't exactly the world you left, usually as a result of wandering away from the Tower while in the Supernal. Things like the acanthus sig character Sunjata, who started his Awakening in the pirate Caribbean, took a wrong turn in Arcadia and arrived in 1990s Boston.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1040843-divination-and-awakening?p=1041165#post1041165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*However*, once an Awakening experience gets underway, it's like banging a gong in the Supernal World of the corresponding Path, and although it's probably not a good idea many mages try to insert themselves as characters in an in-progress Mystery Play. You have to have the right Path and a loose enough grasp of morals to invade someone elses' one direct contact with Truth. The results can be enlightening, or tragic, or tragically enlightening.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1129690-awakening-relics?p=1129794#post1129794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The metaphysics of which should be familiar to those who've read Imperial Mysteries - the Watchtowers project safe-ish areas of the Supernal Realm around them. If you go too far, you run the risk of altering the symbols making up the world and especially your own place in the world, and when you reenter Fallen Reality, you experience what archmasters call Apoenia.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1129690-awakening-relics?p=1129853#post1129853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[Taking a wrong turn in Pandemonium] would probably result in you waking up in Antarctica or something.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1129690-awakening-relics?p=1129931#post1129931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or your sympathetic connections warping. Best friends turned deadly enemies, childhood rivals are now ex-lovers, that sort of thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T17:10:57-07:00","id":1131019,"title":"","content":"I've tried to imagine what a character's Awakening might have been like and how, especially in the case of a plot significant npc, that experience would have shaped them and in my mind it always ends up looking like an Astral journey with over the top Supernal symbols thrown in.<br /> \u200bFor one Mastigos who found himself faced with the decision of whether or not to get involved or continue his comfortable life I had him wake up in the night and go for a walk to clear his head only to find himself walking across violent battlefields representing the wars passed and even some that hadn't happened yet (he was waking up early in WWII) while he himself was contained within a protective glass corridor that eventually led him to a tall tower. The stairs spiraled up the outside of the tower and the top was open, meaning that no matter where he looked he was seeing scenes of the brutality of war. In the center of that room was a stone pillar etched with names and carved into the floor around that old saying about how all that is required for evil to flourish is that good men do nothing. At this point he realized he had a choice, go back to sleep and return to the safety of his life or commit to getting involved, stepping outside of the safety of his glass corridor and doing something about what was happening in the world around him.<br /> <br /> \u200bMy recommendation is try to imagine what sort of journey the Arcanthus would experience, how the thorns of Time and Fate are represented, then pick 'roles' for the witnesses to play. Just like the dream actors in the Astral.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-18T18:43:45-07:00","id":1131055,"title":"","content":"Oooohhhhh, wait. So that means the ''mages who awaken without ever seeing a watchtower'' are being slightly blended with ''your awakening causes apoenia''? That makes a LOT of sense in the context of Imperial Mysteries. It gives unique context to mages who stray from the safety of the traditional awakening with the tower, and makes the watchtowers an interesting Mystery of its own if a mage specializes in awakenings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:10:57-07:00","id":1131303,"title":"","content":"Thank you all for your answers!<br /> <br /> I know SoS is supposed to cover some ground in this affair, but heh, the situation just unfolded itself too early. ^^' The Player's Paths are Thyrsus (Life specialist) and another Acanthus (Time specialist) <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>. The fact that one of them is an Acanthus provides me with the possibility of centering this Awakening in Fate, rather than be redundant about Time. Thus, the idea about blending some Changeling feeling into it, kinda like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6084\" data-vbnamecard=\"6084\">2ptTakrill</a> suggest; all in all, a Journey into Arcadia could very much be represented as a travel by the Edge, although i really don't want to cheapen any game by blending them too closely.<br /> <br /> Those are some really nice quotes, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7593_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7593\" data-vbnamecard=\"7593\">Teatime</a>. They remind me about the Vinca, and the weird and cool Fate effects as seen in that Dark Era writing. Currently, i'm reading IMperial Mysteries in order to capture that elusive Supernal feeling that i sometimes fail to grasp correctly, in my opinion... but i disgress. As i said before thank you all for your answers <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T09:47:38-07:00","id":1131321,"title":"","content":"What abilities (mainly levels of Arcana) do Mages actually have immediately after Awakening? I doubt that they get six dots worth of Arcana right from the start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5973-prometheus","name":"Prometheus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5973_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:13:50-07:00","id":1131332,"title":"","content":"Personally I usually go with one point in both ruling arcana, then rather quickly developing a second point in one of their ruling arcana or a first point in a common arcanum. But there are no official rules for it iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1131211-flintys-homebrew-hub-2e\" target=\"_blank\">My Mage 2e Homebrew</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5241-flinty","name":"Flinty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"793"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-19T10:19:05-07:00","id":1131337,"title":"","content":"There are, it's mentioned in the Mysterium book, I can't remember what it is but the question has been asked dozens of times by now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T03:34:19-07:00","id":1131662,"title":"","content":"I had forget about those Mysterium book rules! I would go with one point in both ruling Arcana, too, but i like to roleplay the Awakening, so i usually end giving 2 dots in the main one, and another point in the other one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}